    },
    {
      "order": 5,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0083",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s04-p095-02040-s001",
      "sentenceText": "In his 1971 book, Aesthetics and Psychobiology, Daniel Berlyne summarized a series of experiments on aesthetic judgments.",
      "sentenceSha256": "fd81e263e1c2f00c58beb7080d93d9928408424228006f272567704c67d299b2",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s04-p095-02040-r001-003",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-041",
      "parentFingerprint": "49efae4af4a410a8a109827097828250c1b3293b3f32b187951fd8ec8ab9a8c2",
      "passageSha256": "edbfc279ac743f0fa98ac36ad89f9f062b12779a222f762b8be4254c867a118a",
      "pdfPages": [
        95
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 6,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0084",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s04-p095-02040-s003",
      "sentenceText": "Simple geometric figures are typically perceived to be more pleasant than complex ones, whereas complex ones are typically perceived to be more interesting than simple ones.",
      "sentenceSha256": "e370bbd03361faf68c5998d67a92db6dc6dc580331725b89c528a4db99ea77a0",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s04-p095-02040-r001-003",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-041",
      "parentFingerprint": "49efae4af4a410a8a109827097828250c1b3293b3f32b187951fd8ec8ab9a8c2",
      "passageSha256": "edbfc279ac743f0fa98ac36ad89f9f062b12779a222f762b8be4254c867a118a",
      "pdfPages": [
        95
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 7,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0085",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s04-p095-03210-s002",
      "sentenceText": "Some figures were simple and symmetrical, some were simple and asymmetrical, some were complex and symmetrical, and the others were complex and asymmetrical.",
      "sentenceSha256": "32510f950d79d70e49429ad4607fb57e02b0ab3aec3201c40b00ca20f5d0f134",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s04-p095-03210-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-042",
      "parentFingerprint": "d643e2df2040942350e312bddff1165c7ff325515d28572c14209a176962c2b2",
      "passageSha256": "d9b6206764020961d41c6bea0c7917e1fab62d99047421b6eb0661421e808e46",
      "pdfPages": [
        95
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 8,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0086",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s04-p095-03210-s003",
      "sentenceText": "Participants rated the simple and symmetrical figures to be the most pleasant, followed by complex and symmetrical, simple and asymmetrical, and complex and asymmetrical.",
      "sentenceSha256": "b69f93b66e5048eae520392bbe2b5e5ef3b364b664ab63da0fc57d53f887fc4f",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s04-p095-03210-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-042",
      "parentFingerprint": "d643e2df2040942350e312bddff1165c7ff325515d28572c14209a176962c2b2",
      "passageSha256": "d9b6206764020961d41c6bea0c7917e1fab62d99047421b6eb0661421e808e46",
      "pdfPages": [
        95
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 9,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0087",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s04-p095-03210-s004",
      "sentenceText": "Symmetry was key to pleasantness.",
      "sentenceSha256": "7879592ecbca2654f3758755a80f14be67b0488b3e2915f5c2f561dc9d0e60e0",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s04-p095-03210-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-042",
      "parentFingerprint": "d643e2df2040942350e312bddff1165c7ff325515d28572c14209a176962c2b2",
      "passageSha256": "d9b6206764020961d41c6bea0c7917e1fab62d99047421b6eb0661421e808e46",
      "pdfPages": [
        95
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 10,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0088",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s04-p095-03210-s006",
      "sentenceText": "Complexity and asymmetry added interestingness, whereas they detracted from pleasantness.",
      "sentenceSha256": "ae6ad744eb50178354b3fbf101992bacbbbba697adfc1ba8ad22576e0318e247",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s04-p095-03210-r005-006",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-043",
      "parentFingerprint": "10775de2f2d74c7da5323b1a4372c59cc466d438bff0cfac72e9f3553924c4bd",
      "passageSha256": "c40dad8efbbb05547a616a12ff26f174e2d134c13982b01ddbb183de681d78c2",
      "pdfPages": [
        95
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 11,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0089",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s04-p095-05550-s001",
      "sentenceText": "More recently, Paul Silvia and Samuel Turner Jr.",
      "sentenceSha256": "bcc2d78e6924de84a102a4a05bef1eea59028b02eac9903e882667bbdf705f6b",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s04-p095-05550-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-044",
      "parentFingerprint": "6b5d7f69408b5151617e15fb3b37fc2be78a93095bf1e4216df13b8598e50964",
      "passageSha256": "ff215b37fe2d89aac720e24b8b907d3331837a22f2047ce4f2ee542996d091f7",
      "pdfPages": [
        95
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 12,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0090",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s04-p095-05550-s002",
      "sentenceText": "conducted an intriguing experiment on aesthetic judgments.",
      "sentenceSha256": "959ce38b3ba27f9f6f943e92828c710dbe8be7e136a321aebd848288fdce3374",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s04-p095-05550-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-044",
      "parentFingerprint": "6b5d7f69408b5151617e15fb3b37fc2be78a93095bf1e4216df13b8598e50964",
      "passageSha256": "ff215b37fe2d89aac720e24b8b907d3331837a22f2047ce4f2ee542996d091f7",
      "pdfPages": [
        95
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 13,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0091",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s04-p095-05550-s005",
      "sentenceText": "These paintings are quite shocking and grotesque, particularly in comparison to the famously serene, warm painting by Monet.",
      "sentenceSha256": "9c0ae59713e5b5d804cd24b286c8ba07d86bc7e455d2a82a05307aea85cac361",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s04-p095-05550-r005-008",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-045",
      "parentFingerprint": "d8123b96298bc8d1d043e14bd5a8232036b95b5d49cf5a31927724f0f432889f",
      "passageSha256": "78093bf2c1666411725e306d3d280e63eebba40e22f9ab01caf492387ea13a6d",
      "pdfPages": [
        95,
        96
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 14,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0092",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s04-p095-05550-s006",
      "sentenceText": "After looking at each painting, participants reported how interesting or uninteresting, boring or engaging, enjoyable or unenjoyable, pleasing or displeasing, comprehensible or incomprehensible, familiar or unfamiliar each painting was.",
      "sentenceSha256": "336d2a88e29fb3717b7fc9d433519a1e3f5e4191a7573a8ffe8bcfed327c5890",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s04-p095-05550-r005-008",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-045",
      "parentFingerprint": "d8123b96298bc8d1d043e14bd5a8232036b95b5d49cf5a31927724f0f432889f",
      "passageSha256": "78093bf2c1666411725e306d3d280e63eebba40e22f9ab01caf492387ea13a6d",
      "pdfPages": [
        95,
        96
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 15,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0093",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s04-p095-05550-s008",
      "sentenceText": "In other words, the easier to understand and simpler the paintings were, the more pleasant they were.",
      "sentenceSha256": "8c97ce4699f1d02eeedcae15ce50615e16887428124a00d15c43872700939be8",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s04-p095-05550-r005-008",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-045",
      "parentFingerprint": "d8123b96298bc8d1d043e14bd5a8232036b95b5d49cf5a31927724f0f432889f",
      "passageSha256": "78093bf2c1666411725e306d3d280e63eebba40e22f9ab01caf492387ea13a6d",
      "pdfPages": [
        95,
        96
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 16,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0094",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s04-p095-05550-s009",
      "sentenceText": "In contrast, interestingness ratings were predicted by disturbingness and unpleasantness.",
      "sentenceSha256": "03a87ddd3a6ef672e14681a4077a29a8750e367735e355c6ee399dcd599f0273",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s04-p095-05550-r009-010",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-046",
      "parentFingerprint": "dfeab37f52f6ce793f0844985d05d9f6a0666ed15466d12b44e46389743d6639",
      "passageSha256": "734c7a7145ef805282982bee798cc78fe97ed5c570a9f866f2fdd4be94e14486",
      "pdfPages": [
        96
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 17,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0095",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s04-p096-02505-s001",
      "sentenceText": "In another experiment, Silvia explored the role of comprehension.",
      "sentenceSha256": "ec0d807152b026714959b739f5c4ce73edc0c6fc5f146fef9ee87abd76286dd1",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s04-p096-02505-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-047",
      "parentFingerprint": "22d49b48193308313e3162bc76e053f46902bbfa01d1a175b98c3e81c0770985",
      "passageSha256": "2ace2c41b687db19c8365dee2a5d0e17e8b6354a503b3559d2bafc8ee53eb898",
      "pdfPages": [
        96
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 18,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0096",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s04-p096-02505-s002",
      "sentenceText": "For instance, participants were asked to read Scott MacLeod’s famously abstract poem The Life of Haifisch.",
      "sentenceSha256": "cb9f4cc90f5bc5ec454c4bd4586e79b803de477a3c1f92fc016951ffdd9018cb",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s04-p096-02505-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-047",
      "parentFingerprint": "22d49b48193308313e3162bc76e053f46902bbfa01d1a175b98c3e81c0770985",
      "passageSha256": "2ace2c41b687db19c8365dee2a5d0e17e8b6354a503b3559d2bafc8ee53eb898",
      "pdfPages": [
        96
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 19,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0097",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s04-p096-02505-s003",
      "sentenceText": "Those who were not provided with any background information could not understand it and did not find it interesting.",
      "sentenceSha256": "7c50d518fe1091a5f847c49dfeb61a384d32a4c73a37c418fd7f53f55bdd6349",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s04-p096-02505-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-047",
      "parentFingerprint": "22d49b48193308313e3162bc76e053f46902bbfa01d1a175b98c3e81c0770985",
      "passageSha256": "2ace2c41b687db19c8365dee2a5d0e17e8b6354a503b3559d2bafc8ee53eb898",
      "pdfPages": [
        96
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 20,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0098",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s04-p096-02505-s005",
      "sentenceText": "There is an intricate line.",
      "sentenceSha256": "8e0521b35ff1642684464f0b6bfb85460dcde927d5f5c1673453a5d09ddd58c9",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s04-p096-02505-r005-006",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-048",
      "parentFingerprint": "5ef22638a81e8f724dda3452bf385ca085fa4f3293c8d3a8defc63df724a095b",
      "passageSha256": "96bea69ac95392995cb98a672a5da3a7679d76b4b04530b20e17ffc4f2aec629",
      "pdfPages": [
        96
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 21,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0099",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s04-p096-04260-s001",
      "sentenceText": "While at the University of Virginia, I had the chance to work with two students, Erin Westgate and Nick Buttrick, with whom I read the existing literature on experimental aesthetics such as Paul Silvia’s.",
      "sentenceSha256": "845cd2c9708f3a562e3b24822c5cc8812fb7a8c67dd86754a4803760aa19a063",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s04-p096-04260-r001-003",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-049",
      "parentFingerprint": "169220808cda0b7acedac7ab657e0ba317f1fb2dbe8b43330251165d761d6294",
      "passageSha256": "4ef57b085282838ca265e0ccd755711682dfdfd857d50fa1ac5a8b7efc3156fb",
      "pdfPages": [
        96
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 22,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0100",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s04-p096-04260-s002",
      "sentenceText": "We wondered if reading all kinds of books early on in life helped readers appreciate more complexity and lead an intellectually rich life.",
      "sentenceSha256": "d9ab6ce11157b03b6c21d884f1b4fa88bd0f61d8ecbca3765661e38dcedb813f",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s04-p096-04260-r001-003",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-049",
      "parentFingerprint": "169220808cda0b7acedac7ab657e0ba317f1fb2dbe8b43330251165d761d6294",
      "passageSha256": "4ef57b085282838ca265e0ccd755711682dfdfd857d50fa1ac5a8b7efc3156fb",
      "pdfPages": [
        96
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 23,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0101",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s04-p096-04260-s004",
      "sentenceText": "We assumed that reading in general would be associated with a more flexible cognitive style and more psychological richness.",
      "sentenceSha256": "5d48704f82efa5b2835d07b0d7654cc3df31d423d0509b0f59a10adada7d941f",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s04-p096-04260-r004-005",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-050",
      "parentFingerprint": "6af32e115f34cb84d066f9ff56bf971460ce1a97c6d7692536a747efff785175",
      "passageSha256": "328c540d5128b2dc10d2c26169b60c6e2b9c3706c4ff2305684d8a62b3fb2a1d",
      "pdfPages": [
        96
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 24,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0102",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s04-p096-06210-s003",
      "sentenceText": "These readers seemed to “essentialize” to a greater degree than those who had read less romance.",
      "sentenceSha256": "88413681c5b3e13515e11bbeaaf5d97f0224d94bbb7a6130e0412c54a6dae124",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s04-p096-06210-r001-003",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-051",
      "parentFingerprint": "3f47fffd1f3c6b775fa7cc29844f9312049d8e41ea67073d96b8dca3af3d34f8",
      "passageSha256": "73923a979755d2cc65344d73df1c03f5e46f6de1ad18ff9333eb7a74303fcd88",
      "pdfPages": [
        96,
        97
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 25,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0103",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s04-p096-06210-s004",
      "sentenceText": "For instance, early romance readers tended to hold a more simplistic view of the world: Joe is a jerk, Jill is an angel, baseball is a bore, opera is for old people, and so on.",
      "sentenceSha256": "7d32524d3483c840d1600e2598663128b89ed146c76113583f3a0b8afcbf8422",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s04-p096-06210-r004-006",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-052",
      "parentFingerprint": "14fdffe8c20bc5d194628bbd660ef4209437d6e30452699e32fb38ca582aff26",
      "passageSha256": "b3e540473e65dcc85569f46910bd947434deabbb123516ec43458ca9a85a8825",
      "pdfPages": [
